course: dictionary
lesson: 1441
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word carrot can mean a vegetable, or it can mean a reward. You find out which by reading the words around it. «Poppy hugs her new bunny and announces: "Snowy's getting a carrot every single day, because rabbits LOVE carrots!"» A bunny eats a carrot, so here it is the orange vegetable.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence and check it still makes sense. «...across the market-place where people throw carrots and jeer...» People throw carrots, which are vegetables, so this is the food meaning. If you swapped in "reward", the sentence would make no sense.
explain: The second meaning is a reward used to make someone do something. Think of the phrase «the carrot and the stick», which means a reward to encourage you, and a punishment to make you move. When the word is about a reward, it is not a real vegetable.
fact: A carrot is a long orange vegetable.
fact: A carrot is the root of a plant that grows under the ground.
fact: A carrot can also be a reward used to make someone do something, as in «the carrot and the stick».
fact: Carrots have vitamin A, which helps keep eyes healthy, but they do not give you night vision.
fact: The plural of carrot is carrots: one carrot, two carrots.
exercise: «Poppy hugs her new bunny and announces: "Snowy's getting a carrot every single day..."» What is a carrot here? | A kind of castle | *A long orange vegetable | A reward used to make someone do something
exercise: The farmer dangled a carrot in front of the horse to make it run faster. What does carrot mean here? | A bunny's toy | A vegetable for lunch | *A reward used to make someone do something | A root under the snow
exercise: Which word is the plural of carrot? | carrot | carrotts | carrotes | *carrots
test: «Sven the reindeer begs for carrots; real reindeer dig through the snow with their broad hooves to eat lichen.» What do real reindeer eat? | *Lichen | Antlers | Snow | Carrots
test: Which phrase uses carrot to mean a reward? | «the carrot patch» | «carrot cake» | *«the carrot and the stick» | «carrot sticks»
exam: In the Second World War, Britain spread the idea that carrots helped pilots see at night. What is the truth? | *Carrots help keep eyes healthy, but they do not give night vision | Carrots give night vision, so pilots could see in the dark | Carrots make eyes glow in the dark | Carrots do nothing at all for eyes
